# CURSOR & AGENT TOKEN OPTIMIZATION RULES

## 1. Just-In-Time Context (JIT) Policy
- **Localized Edits & Bug Fixes**: Always fetch ONLY the specific file or function needed for the issue. Do NOT read unreferenced files or dump the full project tree.
- **Search First**: Use `grep_search` or targeted symbol search to pinpoint exact code blocks before opening files.
- **Targeted Reading**: Inspect only the lines relevant to the bug or feature being modified.

## 2. Repomix & Full Codebase Bundles
- Reserve full codebase bundles or `repomix` dumps strictly for large architectural refactoring requested explicitly by the user.
- Always respect `.repomixignore` to filter out `package-lock.json`, build directories (`dist/`, `graphify-out/`), static images/media, and temporary scripts.

## 3. Circuit Breaker & Verification
- If a tool error repeats twice, halt and re-evaluate rather than looping.
- Run build/deploy/test verification after edits.
